      "full_abstract": "For the annulus 1 < |z| < e, we exhibit a normalized minimal Martin kernel that is strictly below the envelope of normalized positive harmonic functions at every point of a punctured neighborhood of the base point. Four explicit positive harmonic competitors give a uniform first-order gap in every direction. The result disproves the extension to multiply connected domains of the equality-along-a-Green-line property in Hayman and Lingham's Problem 7.42, attributed to Arsove and Johnson. We give direct constructions of the Green and Martin kernels and a proof of minimality. The broader negative conclusion also has a simpler punctured-disc derivation from classical results; our theorem gives a smooth-annulus construction. OpenAI tools were used extensively in developing and independently checking the argument. This note has not undergone human peer review or formal proof-assistant verification.",
      "SEO_title": "Isolated Harnack contact for an annular Martin kernel | Alec Kriebel",
      "meta_description": "An explicit Martin kernel on a smooth annulus has isolated contact with the Harnack envelope, ruling out equality along a Green line issuing from the base point.",
      "title": "A Martin kernel with isolated Harnack contact in an annulus",
      "date": "2026-10-12",
      "version": "1.0.0",
      "native_version_field": "1.0.0",
